{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_buwxaldpw3wlh7m6tn425iakmdsaefznzzf6vtwseh37yn2qe5fq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## What the C library is\n`c_src/` is a single-file library (`src/lib.c`, 956 lines) containing the **stb_ds** implementation (Sean Barrett's dynamic array + hash map) plus two test helpers. Public header `include/lib.h` declares only `intput`, but the CMake build globs the whole file into one `.so`.\n\n## Definition of done — symbol enumeration\nI built the C library with CMake and ran `nm -D`. It exports exactly **16** symbols; my Rust `cdylib` exports the **same 16**, with identical types (`T`) and **zero missing / zero extra**:\n\n`stbds_arrgrowf, stbds_arrfreef, stbds_rand_seed, stbds_hash_string, stbds_hash_bytes, stbds_hmfree_func, stbds_hmget_key_ts, stbds_hmget_key, stbds_hmput_default, stbds_hmput_key, stbds_shmode_func, stbds_hmdel_key, stbds_stralloc, stbds_strreset, strkey, intput`\n\n## Deliverables\n- `translation/Cargo.toml` — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- `translation/src/lib.rs` — 1328 lines, all 16 exports as `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\"`\n- `translation/build.rs` — reproduces the C `__FILE__` used in `assert()` diagnostics\n\n## Fidelity details preserved (not \"fixed\")\n- **`repr(C)` layouts** byte-compatible: `stbds_array_header` (32 B), `stbds_hash_bucket` (128 B), `stbds_hash_index` (104 B), `stbds_string_arena` (24 B, `block`/`mode` at offsets 16/17), 64-byte cache-line alignment of bucket storage, and the `array_header`-before-data / `+elemsize` \"hash pointer\" convention.\n- **libc `realloc`/`free`** used directly (`STBDS_REALLOC`/`STBDS_FREE`), so allocator behavior and pointer ownership are unchanged.\n- **The siphash integer-promotion quirk**: `d[3] << 24` is `int` arithmetic in C, so a high-bit byte makes the value negative and sign-extends into the top 32 bits of `size_t`, clobbering the second half of the word. Reproduced exactly with `i32 → isize → usize` casts rather than \"corrected\" siphash.\n- Other faithful quirks: the no-op `hash ^= hash ^ ROR(...)` lines, the missing `temp_key` assignment in `hmput_key`'s second probe loop, `arrgrowf(NULL, es, 0, 0)` returning `NULL`, `arrfreef` on a raw pointer, `hash_seed` LCG evolution per hash-index creation, and `intput`'s **assertion failures for `num == 9` and `num == 11`** (routed through glibc `__assert_fail` with the same expression text, function, and line 955 → same stderr message and SIGABRT/exit 134).\n\n## Verification (my own, not self-reported by sub-agents)\nTwo `dlopen`-based differential harnesses ran the C `.so` and the Rust `.so` side by side, printing traces that include full internal state (header length/capacity/temp, table slot/used/tombstone counts, seeds, arena state, **and the raw bucket hash/index arrays byte-for-byte**):\n- Structured harness: **4616 lines, 0 diffs** (hashing incl. high-bit and boundary patterns, arrgrowf growth sequences, int maps of size 1→300, 2-int-key maps, all three string-map modes, arena block growth, seed evolution, `strkey`, `intput`).\n- Randomized fuzz (deterministic PRNG, 7 seeds): **~39,200 lines each, 0 diffs**.\n- Abort-path check: identical message/line/exit code for `intput(9)`/`intput(11)`.\n\nScratch build artifacts were removed; `diff -r` confirmed `c_src/` is unmodified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":780,"cache_read_input_tokens":114137,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":780,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e21fcab8-2ac4-4b21-a4be-98151a65b796","uuid":"cd7aada9-f493-431d-9b01-9c0236428556","timestamp":"2026-08-27T10:38:50.631Z"}
